[milestone 46] Implementer summary: Milestone 46 is implemented and verified in real QEMU boot runs. Both `kernel/src/fs.rs` and `kernel/src/main.rs` were changed (no other files touched, no commits made). Summary: `fs.rs` gained a real `FileSystem` trait with two implementations — `DiskFs` (the pre-existing ATA disk logic, moved unchanged into `_disk`-suffixed private functions) and a new `RamFs` (a flat, in-memory `BTreeMap`-backed filesystem). A `resolve_backend()` dispatcher routes any path starting with `ram`/`ram/` to `RamFs` and everything else to `DiskFs`, unchanged. No shell/process/loader code needed to change since they already call the generic `fs::` functions. Two boot-time self-tests (existing `self_test_disk_write` plus new `self_test_ramfs`) both passed in a real QEMU serial log, confirming the old disk path still works and the new ramfs path is reachable through the identical surface and genuinely isolated from disk. Along the way I caught and fixed a real bug in my own first self-test (a filename collision that produced a false isolation failure), documented in `milestones/m46_implement.md` along with the disclosed scope cuts (flat ramfs namespace, no root-listing mount entry, shared 4096-byte cap, not reboot-persistent).

